  "notes": "Combines {遅|おそ}い (late) and {寝|ね} (sleep). Describes going to bed at a late hour, as opposed to {早寝|はやね} (going to bed early). Often used in discussions about sleep habits, health, and children's routines.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {遅寝|おそね}{遅起|おそお}き: going to bed late and getting up late\n- {遅寝|おそね}{早起|はやお}き: going to bed late and getting up early\n- {遅寝|おそね}の{習慣|しゅうかん}: habit of staying up late\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {夜更|よふ}かし: staying up late — more common in everyday conversation, often implies doing something fun\n- {早寝|はやね}: going to bed early — the antonym\n- {寝不足|ねぶそく}: sleep deprivation — the result of not getting enough sleep",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
